On 12/31/22 6:18 PM, Dave McGuire wrote:
> On 12/31/22 18:31, David Holland wrote:
>> I came across PR 22160 today because it had been in feedback since
>> 2008. Apparently on 1.6.1 in 2003, a SCSI TK50 tape drive wasn't
>> working.
>
>   I looked it up; it was filed by John Dundas.  John, are you on this 
> list?  If so, can you describe the setup you were using back then?
>
>             -Dave
>
Dave, et al,

Yes.  The AlphaStation is configured as follows:

AlphaStation 200 (4/233)
SRM V7.0-9
ARC 4.58
PALcode VMS V5.56-2, OSF X1.46-2
Serial ROM 1.3
Diag ROM V1.2
Processor 21064A-6 233 MHz CPU, 512 KB cache
64 MB RAM (4x16MB; 2 slots free)
NCR 810 SCSI controller
CD ROM - RRD43
hard disk: RZ26L-E Rev. B01
Intel SIO 82378
Floppy disk

with PBXGA-AA/AN (ZXLp-E1) graphics board.  A TK50Z-GA was connected to 
the SCSI port.

Hope this helps,

John

